  "measured_on": "2026-10-24",
  "scope": "Design-only principal-file inventory at the unchanged production baseline. Physical lines include comments and blanks; each principal file is assigned once. Forecasts are manual cumulative additions plus deletions, not measured diffs or delivery commitments. The full scenario includes path-scoped local-socket migration, Reno-first core, later BBR/aggregation and qualified exact native UDP transports with explicit bounded-write authority; restricted transports, managed wrappers and external I/O callbacks are excluded. Secondary sites are listed separately without pretending their eventual touched-file count is known. Test/support forecasts include interop adapter, container/dependency pins, CI workflow and case-accounting code/configuration; historical yardsticks keep their original narrower exclusions. Local queue/write timeouts are nonfatal backpressure for ordinary and multipath peers on opted-in endpoints; they do not themselves constitute path failure.",
  "yardstick_method": "Sum git diff --numstat COMMIT^ COMMIT for listed first-parent product commits. Count .go, excluding docs/, benchmarks/, interop/, and mock_ generated files. Production excludes _test.go. Unique filenames per campaign; cumulative added/deleted churn counts repeated edits. Emission excludes E1 feasibility and includes #60 repair. Original BBR excludes Q1 and includes #622 repair. Correction-port is the five #748 port commits only, not all subsequent BBR work.",
